Dual-use security research utility: opencode-codex-security

This plugin connects OpenCode V2 to the OpenAI Codex Security SDK to scan source
repositories for potential vulnerabilities, draft security policies and
statically assess reported findings. It includes deliberately vulnerable local
fixtures for offline demonstrations and automated tests. It does not implement
exploit execution, runtime exploitation, patch application or fix verification.

Intended legitimate use is defensive security review and authorized research on
repositories that the operator owns or has permission to assess. SDK operations
send selected repository source and context to OpenAI for inference; operators
must have permission for that transfer and understand potential costs. Fixture
mode is offline and is not a real assessment. Findings require human review.

Do not use this package for unauthorized access, abuse or malicious activity.
The contentPolicy dual-use declaration and this disclosure must persist across
versions. Automated npm publication uses staging only; a maintainer must review
and approve each staged version with npm two-factor authentication before it is
publicly available. See SECURITY.md for vulnerability reporting.
